# Scratch run output. The CURATED runs under evidence/runs/ are a graded
# deliverable (brief §6.3) and are committed; this stops the other ~700 from
# following them in. `evidence/README.md` indexes the ones that count.
evidence/runs/

# ⛔ `artifacts/*.approved.json` IS NOT IGNORED, and used to be. The rule came
# with a long comment arguing that approval is a person's act so an approved
# artifact should not ship -- sound for a deployed system, wrong here, and the
# comment said so itself while the rule stayed. §6.1 asks for "the exact
# command(s) to run" and every one of them names an approved artifact.
#
# It cost exactly what you would expect: `request_loan.v2.approved.json` was
# created, approved, documented, and never committed, because `git add -A`
# respects .gitignore. A fresh clone got FileNotFoundError on the documented
# demo. The fix at the time was a test that catches the omission; this is the
# fix that removes the trap.
#
# The approval gate is not weakened by this: `assert_replayable` still refuses
# a draft, the approver is still recorded inside the artifact, and a test reads
# every committed file to prove none carries a literal secret.
